    "narrative": "The Austin Waves head into today\u2019s slate with **Gunnar Henderson** anchoring the lineup, carrying an elite score of 81.88. His massive projection is driven by a 16% park adjustment and a 17% SP skill boost against Rea, ensuring he remains a plug-and-play cornerstone despite the category scarcity penalty for his stolen base output. Joining him in the top tier are **Kyle Tucker** (77.36) and **Jackson Merrill** (75.27), both of whom benefit significantly from facing Hughes\u2019 5.19 xERA. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** also projects as a high-floor play (73.66) against Arrighetti, capitalizing on a 14% platoon edge that makes him our primary leverage point against the Houston rotation.\n\nWhile **Gunnar Henderson** and the outfield trio define our ceiling, the most complex decision occurred at the fringe of the starting nine, where **Brayan Rocchio** was our highest-graded bench option at 51.40. **Brayan Rocchio** narrowly missed the cut because the optimizer favored the higher raw efficiency of **Drake Baldwin** (53.01) and **Miguel Vargas** (53.76), despite the latter facing a tougher southpaw matchup against Bennett. Investors should note the risk surrounding **Heliot Ramos**; despite his 1.000 recency score, his 43.02 rating against Cease is depressed by a 19% SP skill penalty, placing him at the threshold of a benching. Furthermore, with lineups pending for **Jackson Merrill**, **Kyle Tucker**, and **Andy Pages**, we are monitoring potential order shifts that could oscillate their scores by several points, though their favorable matchup against Hughes provides a sufficient cushion to keep them locked into the starting slots.",
